Phase 3③ follow-up — incidents partitioned by tenant, verified end to end
==========================================================================
Date : 2026-07-28
Mode : built artifact (`next build` + `next start`), stub on-prem incident source


The write gap under the read gap
---------------------------------
`/api/dashboard/incidents` returned every tenant's incidents to anyone. It could
not be partitioned because the tenant was never stored: `NormalizedIncident` has
carried `tenant`/`env` as first-class fields since Phase 1a, and
`_record_incident` dropped them at write time. The read gap and the write gap
were the same gap; the read side is merely where it got noticed.

Fixed at both ends. `tenant`/`env` are written only when non-empty — absent and
`""` are different facts, and writing `""` would make every legacy row look like
a real tenant named nothing.


Why the granted-viewer path had never been verified
-----------------------------------------------------
The local-dev auth bypass hardcoded `role: "admin"` and `username: "local-dev"`.
The only session obtainable without real GitHub OAuth was therefore the one role
that skips every check — so the entire authorization surface (roles, tenant
grants, partitioned reads) was locally unexercisable. That is why this
verification stayed owed.

The bypass now resolves the role from the same user record a real sign-in reads.
`DASHBOARD_DEV_AUTH_USER` selects who you sign in as; the default `local-dev`
stays admin so existing local setups are unchanged, and an unknown user gets the
least privilege rather than the most.


Fixture
--------
Three incidents from a stub on-prem source:
    INC-ACME-1    tenant=acme
    INC-GLOBEX-1  tenant=globex
    INC-LEGACY-1  (no tenant — stands in for rows written before the fix)

`viewer-demo` is granted `["acme"]` in the user record.


Live round trips
-----------------
    ANONYMOUS (no session)
      ids: []            restricted: True   withheld: 3

    VIEWER-DEMO (role=viewer, grant=['acme'])
      session : username=viewer-demo role=viewer
      ids     : ['INC-ACME-1']
      tenants : ['acme']
      restricted: False  withheld: 2
      cache-control: private, no-store

    ADMIN (default local-dev)
      session : role=admin
      ids     : ['INC-GLOBEX-1', 'INC-ACME-1', 'INC-LEGACY-1']
      restricted: False  withheld: 0

The viewer sees one of three. The neighbour's incident and the untagged legacy
row are both withheld, and the count says so rather than the list just being
shorter. The admin sees all three including the untagged one.

The cache header is part of the result, not decoration: the response now varies
by caller, so the previous `public, s-maxage=30` would have let a shared cache
serve one tenant's incidents to another.


Falsification
--------------
Injecting the obvious wrong default — treat "no tenant recorded" as visible to
everyone — failed all three RowFiltering tests; restoring passed them.


WHAT IS STILL OPEN
-------------------
- **deployments / activities remain unpartitioned, and for a different reason.**
  Incidents had a tenant and dropped it. Deployments never had one: the record
  carries `provider/service/version/environment`, where `environment` is a free
  string ("production"), not the registry's tenant/env pair. Partitioning them
  needs a data-model decision about what tenant owns a deployment — that is
  design work, not a bug fix, so nothing was invented here.
- Do not describe the dashboard as tenant-isolated. Two read paths are
  partitioned (fleet, incidents); the rest are not.
